  "description": "Reid Vantage 2 | Endurance road bike\nFast, capable and built for longer rides – an endurance road bike designed for road cycling, fitness and exploring beyond smooth tarmac.\nThe Reid Bikes Vantage 2 combines a lightweight aluminium frame, full carbon fibre fork and Shimano CUES components to deliver reliable performance and comfort across varied routes. Its endurance-focused geometry makes it a versatile choice for riders looking to cover longer distances, improve their fitness or take on new road adventures.\nThe double-butted hydroformed aluminium frame features fully integrated cable routing and a 12mm thru-axle for a clean finish and secure handling. Its updated geometry provides a more comfortable riding position, while the specially designed ovalised seatstays help absorb road vibrations and reduce fatigue on longer rides.\nA Shimano CUES 20-speed drivetrain offers a wide gear range for tackling climbs and maintaining momentum on flatter roads. The compact 50/34T chainset is paired with an 11-39T cassette, providing versatile gearing for different gradients and riding conditions.\nTektro C550 dual-piston mechanical disc brakes with 160mm rotors deliver dependable stopping power and control. The full carbon fibre fork helps reduce weight and absorb road vibrations, while 700c alloy wheels fitted with Kenda Kriterium 700x30mm tyres provide a balance of rolling efficiency and road comfort.\nFinished with compact alloy drop handlebars, comfortable bar tape and a sport saddle, the Reid Bikes Vantage 2 combines considered design with practical components for everyday road riding and longer adventures.\nThe Reid Bikes Vantage 2 is ideal for:\n\nEndurance road cycling, with comfort-focused geometry for longer days in the saddle\n\nFitness and recreational riding, with a lightweight frame and responsive handling\n\nTackling varied routes, with Shimano CUES 20-speed gearing and a wide-range cassette\n\nClimbing and descents, with versatile gearing and dependable Tektro disc brakes\n\nRoad comfort, with a full carbon fibre fork and vibration-reducing seatstay design\n\nExploring beyond smooth tarmac, with 700x30mm tyres suited to paved roads and firmer surfaces",
